# Intentionally empty: the `work` profile has no 1Password, so nothing
# OS-specific is needed here.
#
# No `gpg.ssh.program` and no `core.sshCommand`, on purpose. Commit signing
# stays on (commit.gpgsign and gpg.format = ssh in ~/.gitconfig) and git signs
# with its default ssh-keygen. The key comes only from ~/.gitconfig.local,
# which is untracked and per machine.
#
# The file has to exist: the tracked ~/.gitconfig includes ~/.gitconfig-os
# unconditionally, and on Windows a stale ~/.gitconfig-os link from a previous
# `personal` run is only replaced by pointing it at something real.
